# Build output
/dist/
/.build/
*.zip

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Python bytecode — the checkers are scripts, and their .pyc is a build artefact of running them
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Never commit these
*.pem
*.key
.env

# Machine-specific values (paths, mounts): right here, wrong on any other machine.
tools/machine.env

# Claude Code's own scratch, same rule one layer up: the granted permissions belong to this machine,
# and a worktree is a second checkout its tooling makes and forgets. Left untracked they are not
# merely untidy - `release.sh` refuses a dirty tree, so an artefact of the tools would block a
# release. Named one by one rather than ignoring `.claude/` whole: anything shared put there later
# should be visible, not silently swallowed.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
